<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48552" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">torcŭlar</span></b> , āris,
			n.
		torqueo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A press</i> used in making wine or oil, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 26, 62, §
			230</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A cellar for storing up oil</i>, <i>an
				oil-cellar</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 6, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 52, 10</span></i> sq.;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				15, 1, 2, § 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 3, 3, §
			10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
